**
!dist/**
!media/**
!README.md
!LICENSE
!package.json
!package.nls*.json
!l10n/**
!provenance.json

# t-09a462 — node-pty is `external` in esbuild (a native addon cannot be bundled), so the extension
# host `require()`s it at runtime from node_modules. Nothing re-included it here, so every installed
# build shipped without it and the agent pane could never attach: "Cannot find module 'node-pty'".
#
# Only NEGATIONS below, never a re-exclusion inside a negated tree. `.vscodeignore` does not honour
# that shape — t-009d2f is the incident: `dist/webview-preview/**` sat here as a documented, dead
# exclusion after `!dist/**` and shipped ~274KB of dev harness for weeks. So the debug symbols are
# left out by NOT naming them, not by excluding them: node-pty's Windows .pdb files are 58MB, while
# every platform's real binary together is 4MB.
#
# node-pty resolves its own binary at runtime (lib/utils.js: build/Release, then build/Debug, then
# prebuilds/<platform>-<arch>), so shipping every platform's payload lets one VSIX serve all of them
# — no per-platform packaging. The host's own build output covers the platform this was built on
# (Linux builds from source; there is no linux entry under prebuilds/).
!node_modules/node-pty/package.json
!node_modules/node-pty/lib/**
!node_modules/node-pty/build/Release/*.node
!node_modules/node-pty/prebuilds/**/*.node
!node_modules/node-pty/prebuilds/**/conpty/**
